# 1. Stable Project Baselines

## Data Hub

The Data Hub module is:

- Fully completed
- Production verified
- Human-QA approved
- Merged into `main`
- Deployed
- Officially closed
- CLOSED AND FROZEN

Do not:

- Reopen Data Hub
- Redesign Data Hub
- Refactor Data Hub
- Modify Data Hub
- Include Data Hub in unrelated commits
- Use Data Hub as a test area
- Re-audit Data Hub without an explicit request

Data Hub may only be inspected in read-only mode when another module depends
on its existing contracts, database structures, ACL, scheduler patterns,
runtime state, design tokens or APIs.

## AI Shared Foundation

The broad shared AI runtime foundation is CLOSED AND FROZEN unless a
reproduced defect requires a separate, explicitly approved Foundation Work
Package.

The foundation includes:

- Authentication hardening
- Capability authorization
- Agent execution policy
- Requested versus effective runtime mode
- Emergency Kill Switch
- Worker acknowledgement
- Scheduler execution path
- Demo/Dry-Run enforcement
- Route security
- Redis safety
- Agent panel RTL and Persian typography
- Analytical scheduler separation
- Staging readiness
- Browser automation

## Agents Shell

Agents Shell is CLOSED AND FROZEN.

Do not reopen or redesign the shared AI runtime foundation or Agents Shell
without:

- A reproduced defect
- A scoped RCA
- Explicit approval
- Targeted regression requirements

## Closed Baseline Rule

A closed baseline may be inspected in read-only mode.

A closed baseline may be changed only when:

1. A defect is reproduced
2. The defect cannot be correctly fixed outside the baseline
3. The smallest affected shared surface is identified
4. Regression consumers are listed
5. Explicit implementation approval is granted
6. The baseline is re-closed after Human QA

A safe additive shared-token extension is allowed only when:

- Existing token values do not change
- Existing consumers do not change behavior
- New consumers are listed
- Browser regression covers existing consumers
- The change is documented as additive

