# 7. Vertical Slice Definition

A complete vertical slice includes every affected layer of one clearly
defined outcome:

User
→ UI
→ Frontend state
→ API client
→ Backend route
→ Validation
→ Authentication
→ Capability/RBAC/ACL
→ Runtime policy
→ Business service
→ Provider adapter where applicable
→ Database
→ Redis/cache
→ Worker/scheduler where applicable
→ Audit/history
→ UI refresh
→ Browser QA
→ Human QA
→ Deployment
→ Git closeout

A slice is not complete if only one required layer is fixed.

Examples of incomplete work:

- UI-only fix for a backend defect
- Route-only authorization patch with an unsafe legacy path still mounted
- Database migration without the business workflow
- Backend endpoint without a usable UI
- UI redesign using fake or contradictory data
- Tests not executed
- Code committed but not deployed
- Deployment without checking the served artifact
- Cursor report without Human QA when Human QA is required

A slice may intentionally omit layers marked NOT APPLICABLE, but the report
must explain why.

